  "title": "82: al-Infetaar الإنفطار",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاِذَا السَّمَآءُ انْفَطَرَتْۙ‏(1)\nEZAS SAMAAA-UN FATARAT.\nWhen the sky is rent apart,\nوَاِذَا الْكَوَاكِبُ انْتَثَرَتْۙ‏(2)\nWA EZAL KAWAAKEBUN TASARAT.\nwhen the stars are scattered,\nوَاِذَا الْبِحَارُ فُجِّرَتْۙ‏(3)\nWA EZAL BEHAARO FUJJERAT.\nwhen the seas are merged,\nوَاِذَا الْقُبُوْرُ بُعْثِرَتْۙ‏(4)\nWA EZAL QOBOORO BO’SERAT.\nwhen the graves are overturned,\nعَلِمَتْ نَفْسٌ مَّا قَدَّمَتْ وَاَخَّرَتْؕ‏(5)\nA’LEMAT NAFSUM MAA QADDAMAT WA AKHKHARAT.\nthen a soul shall know what it has sent ahead and left behind.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الْاِنْسَانُ مَا غَرَّكَ بِرَبِّكَ الْكَرِيْمِۙ‏(6)\nYAA AYYOHAL INSAANO MAA GHARRAKA BE-RABBEKAL KAREEMIL.\nO man! What has deceived you about your generous Lord,\nالَّذِىْ خَلَقَكَ فَسَوّٰٮكَ فَعَدَلَكَۙ‏(7)\nLAZEE KHALAQAKA FA-SAWWAAKA FA-A’DALAKA.\nwho created you and proportioned you, and gave you an upright nature,\nفِىْۤ اَىِّ صُوْرَةٍ مَّا شَآءَ رَكَّبَكَؕ‏(8)\nFEE AYYE SOORATIM MAA SHAAA-A RAKKABAK.\nand composed you in any form that He wished?\nكَلَّا بَلْ تُكَذِّبُوْنَ بِالدِّيْنِۙ‏(9)\nKALLAA BAL TOKAZZEBOONA BID-DEENE.\nNo! Indeed, you deny the Retribution.\nوَاِنَّ عَلَيْكُمْ لَحٰفِظِيْنَۙ‏(10)\nWA INNA A’LAYKUM LA-HAAFEZEENA.\nIndeed, there are over you watchers,\nكِرَامًا كَاتِبِيْنَۙ‏(11)\nKERAAMAN KAATEBEENA.\nnoble writers,\nيَعْلَمُوْنَ مَا تَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(12)\nYA’LAMOONA MAA TAF-A’LOON.\nwho know whatever you do.\nاِنَّ الْاَبْرَارَ لَفِىْ نَعِيْمٍۚ‏(13)\nINNAL ABRAARA LAFEE NA-E’EM.\nIndeed the pious shall be amid bliss,\nوَاِنَّ الْفُجَّارَ لَفِىْ جَحِيْمٍ ۚۖ‏(14)\nWA INNAL FUJJAARA LAFEE JAHEEMIN-Y.\nand indeed the vicious shall be in hell,\nيَّصْلَوْنَهَا يَوْمَ الدِّيْنِ‏(15)\nYASLAWNAHAA YAWMAD DEEN.\nentering it on the Day of Retribution,\nوَمَا هُمْ عَنْهَا بِغَآئِبِيْنَؕ‏(16)\nWA MAA HUM A’NHAA BE-GHAAA-EBEEN.\nand they shall not be absent from it.\nوَمَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا يَوْمُ الدِّيْنِۙ‏(17)\nWA MAA ADRAAKA MAA YAWMUD DEENE.\nAnd what will show you what is the Day of Retribution?\nثُمَّ مَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكَ مَا يَوْمُ الدِّيْنِؕ‏(18)\nSUMMA MAA ADRAAKA MAA YAWMUD DEEN.\nAgain, what will show you what is the Day of Retribution?\nيَوْمَ لَا تَمْلِكُ نَفْسٌ لِّنَفْسٍ شَيْئًا‌ ؕ وَالْاَمْرُ يَوْمَئِذٍ لِّلَّهِ‏(19)\nYAWMA LAA TAMLEKO NAFSUL LE-NAFSIN SHAY-AA, WAL AMRO YAWMA-EZIL LILLAAH.\nIt is a day when no soul will be of any avail to another soul and all command that day will belong to Allah.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Infetaar (The Cleaving Asunder)\nThere are 19 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that if a person recites this Surah frequently in his prayers then on the Day of Judgement there will be no curtain between Allah (s.w.t.) and himself and when his book of deeds will be opened, Allah (s.w.t.) will protect him from humiliation.\nIf a prisoner writes this Surah and keeps it with him, he will be released sooner and he will be saved from any dangers. It is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that even if the sins of the one who recites this Surah are equal to the drops of rain, he will still be forgiven. This Surah is also good for the eyes and one should blow gently into the eyes after reciting this Surah."
